    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0117" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/148<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >1/12</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-24T20:00:00-05:00">May 24, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 25—12:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. The Provisional President<anchor n="44" xml:id="d124-f1"/> approves plan
                    outlined in Department’s No. 46, May 23, noon,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d124-f2"/>
                    and will be pleased to receive emissaries. Secrecy emphasized as per
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
